  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rehabilitation and Extension of the Chishimba Falls Hydropower Plant</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Rehabilitierung und Erweiterung des Wasserkraftwerks Chishimba Falls</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">CO2-schonender Ausbau der Energieerzeugungskapazit&#xe4;ten von Sambia</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Chishimba Falls small hydropower plant is located in Zambias Northern Province, one of the poorest regions in the country. The HPP was built between the 1950s and 1970s and serves to secure the power supply for the provincial capital Kasama and the surrounding regions, which currently only receive an unreliable power supply via the national grid. Due to signs of aging, the power plant can currently only generate around 4.2 MW instead of its installed capacity of 6 MW. The project aims to rehabilitate and expand the hydroelectric power plant to 15 MW in order to improve the power supply in the long term, reduce the use of diesel generators, and promote economic development and poverty reduction in the region. The project includes the modernization of existing facilities as well as environmental and social measures, thereby contributing to a more stable and environmentally friendly power grid in northern Zambia.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Das Kleinwasserkraftwerk (WKW) Chishimba Falls befindet sich in der Northern Province Sambias, einer der &#xe4;rmsten Regionen des Landes. Das WKW wurde zwischen den 1950er und 1970er Jahren erbaut und dient dazu, die Stromversorgung der Provinzhauptstadt Kasama und der umliegenden Regionen zu sichern, die derzeit nur eine unzuverl&#xe4;ssige Stromversorgung &#xfc;ber das nationale Netz erhalten. Aufgrund der Alterserscheinungen kann das Kraftwerk aktuell nur etwa 4,2 MW statt der installierten 6 MW Leistung erzeugen. Das Vorhaben sieht die Rehabilitierung und Erweiterung des WKW auf 15 MW vor, um die Stromversorgung nachhaltig zu verbessern, den Einsatz von Dieselgeneratoren zu reduzieren und die wirtschaftliche Entwicklung sowie die Armutsbek&#xe4;mpfung in der Region zu f&#xf6;rdern. Das Projekt umfasst die Modernisierung der bestehenden Anlagen sowie Umwelt- und Sozialma&#xdf;nahmen und tr&#xe4;gt so zu einem stabileren und umweltfreundlicheren Stromnetz in Nord-Sambia bei.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Chishimba Falls small hydropower plant is located in Zambias Northern Province, one of the poorest regions in the country. The HPP was built between the 1950s and 1970s and serves to secure the power supply for the provincial capital Kasama and the surrounding regions, which currently only receive an unreliable power supply via the national grid. Due to signs of aging, the power plant can currently only generate around 4.2 MW instead of its installed capacity of 6 MW. The project aims to rehabilitate and expand the hydroelectric power plant to 15 MW in order to improve the power supply in the long term, reduce the use of diesel generators, and promote economic development and poverty reduction in the region. The project includes the modernization of existing facilities as well as environmental and social measures, thereby contributing to a more stable and environmentally friendly power grid in northern Zambia.</narrative>
  </description>
